'''Presidential elections''' were held in [[Turkey]] on 10 August 2014.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.reuters.com/article/2014/03/07/us-turkey-election-idUSBREA2610R20140307 |title=Turkey sets Aug 10 for presidential election: source |accessdate=21 March 2014 |publisher=}}</ref> The result was a victory for the incumbent Prime Minister [[Recep Tayyip Erdoğan]], who was elected by a majority of the vote.  

==Background==
The Law on Presidential Elections accepted and put into effect on 20 January 2012 decided that presidential elections will be held in 2014 instead of 2012; within 60 days before the end of the seven-year term of incumbent [[President of Turkey]] [[Abdullah Gül]], who will be the last indirectly elected [[President of Turkey]]. As Gül took office on 28 August 2007, the first possible day could be 29 June, but a date between 10 and 17 August is considered more reasonable.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.turkiyegazetesi.com.tr/gundem/123967.aspx |language=Turkish |title=Cumhurbaşkanı seçimi ağustos başı yapılacak |accessdate=5 March 2014 |publisher=}}</ref>

It was decided in the same law that former presidents [[Kenan Evren]], [[Süleyman Demirel]], [[Ahmet Necdet Sezer]] and incumbent [[Abdullah Gül]] could not be nominated for a second term, but this was ruled unconstitutional by the [[Constitutional Court of Turkey]], allowing them to run for a second term. Also, the [[Prime Minister of Turkey]] could be nominated for the presidency without having to resign from his post.

The presidential elections campaign were declared to be held in an "American manner", where candidates could accept personal donations for their campaigns; however, one person could not donate more than 8,259 TL (approximately US$4,500) to a campaign.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://siyaset.milliyet.com.tr/cankaya-yasasi-meclis-ten-gecti/siyaset/siyasetdetay/20.01.2012/1491396/default.htm |language=Turkish |title=Çankaya yasası Meclis'ten geçti |accessdate=2 September 2012 |publisher=}}</ref>

==Official candidates==
* [[Recep Tayyip Erdoğan]], incumbent [[Prime Minister of Turkey]]<ref name="todayszaman1">{{cite news|url=http://www.todayszaman.com/news-350260-pm-as-candidate-for-president-may-receive-half-of-overseas-vote.html|title=PM as candidate for president may receive half of overseas vote|work=[[Today's Zaman]]|date=14 June 2014|accessdate=21 June 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.aa.com.tr/en/news/322653--turkeys-deputy-pm-backs-erdogan-for-president|title=Turkey's Deputy PM backs Erdogan for president|work=[[Anadolu Agency]]|date=4 May 2014|accessdate=21 June 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Çevik |first=İlnur |date=10 May 2014 |title=Can the opposition have any change against Erdogan?|url=http://www.dailysabah.com/columns/ilnur-cevik/2014/05/10/does-the-opposition-have-any-chance-against-erdogan |newspaper=Daily Sabah|location=Balmumcu, Istanbul |publisher=[[Sabah (newspaper)|Sabah]]}}</ref>
* [[Ekmeleddin İhsanoğlu]], former Secretary-General of the [[Organisation of Islamic Cooperation]] (Nominated by [[Republican People's Party (Turkey)|CHP]] and [[Nationalist Movement Party|MHP]],<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.ft.com/intl/cms/s/0/4a9a34d2-f570-11e3-be21-00144feabdc0.html#axzz35H7qgjn9|title=Turkey's opposition choose joint presidential candidate|work=[[Financial Times]]|date=16 June 2014|accessdate=21 June 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.hurriyetdailynews.com/turkeys-main-opposition-parties-to-nominate-ex-head-of-islamic-body-ihsanoglu-for-presidency.aspx?pageID=238&nID=67850&NewsCatID=338|title=Turkey's main opposition parties to nominate ex-head of Islamic body İhsanoğlu for presidency|work=[[Hürriyet Daily News]]|date=16 June 2014|accessdate=21 June 2014}}</ref> <br/ > Supported by [[Democratic Party (Turkey, current)|DP]], [[Democratic Left Party (Turkey)|DSP]], [[Independent Turkey Party|BTP]],<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.ntvmsnbc.com/id/25524244|title=5 partiden 'çatı aday'a destek|work=[[NTV (Turkey)|NTV]]|date=2 July 2014|accessdate=2 July 2014}}</ref> [[Liberal Democratic Party (Turkey)|LDP]]<ref>{{cite news|url=http://188.95.146.137/news/LDP-Ihsanoglu-na-destek-karari-aldi_1407-CHMTQ5MTQwNy8xMDA1|title=LDP, İhsanoğlu'na destek kararı aldı|work=[[Cihan News Agency]]|date=1 July 2014|accessdate=7 July 2014}}</ref> and [[Great Union Party|BBP]]<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.aa.com.tr/tr/haberler/359575--bbp-ihsanoglunu-destekleme-karari-aldi|title=BBP İhsanoğlu'nu destekleme kararı aldı|work=[[Anadolu News Agency]]|date=16 July 2014|accessdate=16 July 2014}}</ref>)
* [[Selahattin Demirtaş]], leader of [[Peoples' Democratic Party (Turkey)|Peoples' Democratic Party]]<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.cnnturk.com/haber/turkiye/selahattin-demirtas-hdpnin-cumhurbaskani-adayi-mi|title=Selahattin Demirtaş HDP'nin cumhurbaşkanı adayı mı?|work=[[CNN Turk]]|date=18 June 2014|accessdate=21 June 2014}}</ref>

==Campaigns==

The campaigns of all three candidates centred mainly on the [[Israel–Gaza conflict|2014 Israel–Gaza conflict]], the peace process with [[PKK]] rebels, the [[Gezi Park protests]] and 17 December 2013 [[2013 corruption scandal in Turkey|government corruption scandal]]

===Erdoğan campaign===
[[File:Erdoğan (2014 cumhurbaşkanlığı seçim logosu).png|thumb|Erdoğan's campaign logo]]
Incumbent Prime Minister Recep Tayyip Erdoğan formally announced his candidacy for the Presidency on 1 July 2014 in a speech that lasted just over an hour.<ref>{{cite news|title=AK Parti'nin cumhurbaşkanı adayı Recep Tayyip Erdoğan|url=http://www.cnnturk.com/haber/turkiye/ak-partinin-cumhurbaskani-adayi-recep-tayyip-erdogan|accessdate=3 August 2014|work=CNN Türk|agency=1 July 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|title=AK Parti'nin cumhurbaşkanı adayı Recep Tayyip Erdoğan|url=http://www.hurriyet.com.tr/gundem/26719347.asp|accessdate=3 August 2014|work=Hürriyet|agency=1 July 2014}}</ref> Speculation that he would be the AK Party's candidate was widespread long before the announcement.<ref>{{cite news|title=Erdoşan's candidacy for presidency to be announced 1st July|url=http://en.protothema.gr/turkey-erdogans-candidacy-for-president-to-be-announced-on-1st-of-july/|accessdate=3 August 2014|work=Protothema News|agency=24 June 2014}}</ref><ref>[http://www.dailystar.com.lb/News/Middle-East/2014/Jun-22/261109-turkey-pm-erdogan-says-ak-party-is-not-one-mans-party ]{{dead link|date=August 2014}}</ref> On the same day, the Erdoğan logo was unveiled, and received criticism for bearing resemblance to the [[Barack Obama|Obama]] [[United States presidential election, 2008|2008 presidential election]] campaign logo, as well as the ''Holiday Place'' logo.<ref>{{cite web|author=7 August 2014 5:56 pm EDT |url=http://www.huffingtonpost.com/alparslan-akku/erdogans-presidential-cam_b_5567633.html |title=Erdogan's Presidential Campaign Bears a Logo &#124; Alparslan Akkuş |publisher=Huffingtonpost.com |date=}}</ref> A tweet from the [[Ministry of Finance (Turkey)|finance minister]], [[Mehmet Şimşek]], which claimed that the logo has [[Islamic calligraphy|Arabic calligraphy]] of the [[Muhammad|Prophet Muhammad's]] name also sparked debate over the use of religion in the political campaign.<ref name="todayszaman2">{{cite web|url=http://www.todayszaman.com/news-352346-erdogans-logo-ignites-debate-over-political-abuses-of-religion.html |title=Erdoğan's logo ignites debate over political abuses of religion |publisher=Todayszaman.com |date=7 July 2014}}</ref> Erdoğan's campaign slogan is "''Milli İrade, Milli Güç, Hedef 2023''" (''National Will, National Strength, Target 2023''). On 11 July, Erdoğan unveiled a new campaign song and slogan, "''Yeni Türkiye Yolunda Demokrasi, Refah, İtibar''" (''Democracy, Prosperity and Prestige on the Road to a New Turkey'').<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.internethaber.com/iste-erdoganin-secim-slogani-696355h.htm |title=İşte Erdoğan'ın seçim sloganı! haberi |publisher=Internethaber.com |date=}}</ref>

Erdoğan's campaign has been dominated by electoral rallies, beginning in [[Samsun]] on 5 July and then moving to [[Erzurum]], mimicking [[Mustafa Kemal Atatürk]]'s route which he took at the start of the [[Turkish War of Independence]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.beyazgazete.com/video/webtv/siyaset-3/cumhurbaskani-adayi-ve-basbakan-erdogan-in-samsun-mitingi-427047.html |title=Cumhurbaşkanı adayı ve Başbakan Erdoğan'ın Samsun Mitingi |publisher=Beyazgazete.com |date=}}</ref> His rally speeches mainly centred on his achievements as Prime Minister and also contained frequent attacks on both the opposition as well as [[Fethullah Gülen]], the leader of the [[Hizmet]] Movement living in [[Pennsylvania]]. During his [[Hatay]] rally on 21 July, he accused Gülen of not speaking out on behalf of the [[Palestinian people|Palestinians]] in [[Gaza]] and accused [[Israel]] of "following in the footsteps of [[Hitler]]".<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.ajanskonya.net/siyaset/recep-tayyip-erdogan-hatay-mitingi-konusmasinda-h48196.html |title=Recep Tayyip Erdoğan Hatay Mitingi Konuşmasında |publisher=Ajanskonya.net |date=}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.ensonhaber.com/basbakan-erdoganin-hatay-mitingi-konusmasi-2014-03-22.html |title=Başbakan Erdoğan'ın Hatay mitingi konuşması İZLE |publisher=En son haber |date=22 March 2014}}</ref> During his [[Kahramanmaraş]] rally on 1 August, he claimed that the opposition CHP was supporting Israel during the Gaza crisis.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.aa.com.tr/tr/politika/367381--basbakan-erdogan-kahramanmarasta |title=CHP Hitler'in izinden giden İsrail'e sahip çıkıyor – Anadolu Ajansı |publisher=Aa.com.tr |date=}}</ref>

During his electoral rally in [[Van (Turkey)|Van]], Erdoğan attacked his rival Ekmeleddin İhsanoğlu for allegedly mistaking the [[Independence March]], the Turkish [[National Anthem]], for a poem composed for the fallen soldiers at [[Çanakkale]] during the [[Gallipoli Campaign]]. In his [[Kahramanmaraş]] rally on 1 August, he showed the crowd a video of İhsanoğlu misreading the Independence March.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.milliyet.com.tr/basbakan-kahramanmaras-ta-konusuyor/siyaset/detay/1919657/default.htm |title=Erdoğan İhsanoğlu'nu bu görüntülerle vurdu – Milliyet Haber |publisher=Milliyet.com.tr |date=}}</ref>

In addition to his electoral rallies, AK Party activists have also launched a door-to-door operation in order to gather support by delivering food, clothing and other items to families. According to the [[OSCE]], the Erdoğan campaign has also organised [[iftar]] tents during the month of [[Ramadan]] and has distributed toys and women's scarves at electoral rallies.<ref name="hurriyetdailynews.com">{{cite web|url=http://www.hurriyetdailynews.com/osce-slams-use-of-public-funds-for-turkish-pm-erdogans-presidential-campaign.aspx?pageID=238&nID=69880&NewsCatID=338 |title=OSCE slams use of public funds for Turkish PM Erdoğan's presidential campaign – POLITICS |publisher=Hurriyetdailynews.com |date=13 September 2011}}</ref> On 15 July 2014, the government began a huge distribution of free coal to families in [[İzmir]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://gundem.bugun.com.tr/secim-oncesi-bedava-komur-dagitimi-haberi/1187562 |title=İzmir'de seçim öncesi bedava kömür dağıtımı |publisher=Gundem.bugun.com.tr |date=}}</ref>

===İhsanoğlu campaign===
[[Ekmeleddin İhsanoğlu]] was announced as the joint candidate of the [[Republican People's Party (Turkey)|Republican People's Party]] (CHP) and the [[Nationalist Movement Party]] (MHP) on 16 June 2014.<ref>[http://www.haberturk.com/polemik/haber/958500-chp-ve-mhpnin-cati-adayi-belli-oldu-ekmeleddin-ihsanoglu-kimdir ]{{dead link|date=August 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.sabah.com.tr/Gundem/2014/06/16/iste-muhalefetin-kosk-adayi |title=Muhafeletin "çatı adayı" belli oldu-Sabah – 16 Haziran 2014 |publisher=Sabah.com.tr |date=16 June 2014}}</ref> The decision drew criticism from many CHP supporters due to his former role as Secretary General of the [[Organisation of Islamic Cooperation]], which some members of the CHP saw as an organisation which lacked secular and [[Kemalist]] credentials.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.radikal.com.tr/politika/ekmeleddin_ihsanoglu_ataturk_ve_cumhuriyet_dusmani_mi-1197651 |title=Ekmeleddin İhsanoğlu, Atatürk ve Cumhuriyet düşmanı mı? – Politika Haberleri |publisher=Radikal |date=18 June 2014}}</ref> An opinion poll on show of 23 Juneed that only 32% of CHP supporters were happy with their party's choice of candidate, compared to 75% of MHP supporters. Meanwhile, 68% of CHP supporters were dissatisfied with the decision, compared to only 25% of MHP supporters.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.ilk-kursun.com/haber/186271/cati-adayli-ilk-secim-anketi/ |title="Çatı aday"lı ilk seçim anketi – İlk Kurşun Gazetesi |publisher=Ilk-kursun.com |date=}}</ref> In response to the controversy over his secular credentials, İhsanoğlu stated on 26 June that he thought of [[Mustafa Kemal Atatürk]] as a "national hero" and that he had defended secularism in many of his books.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QJDNG-CNCrg |title=Kemal Kılıçdaroğlu ve Ekmeleddin İhsanoğlu Ortak Basın Toplantısı Yaptı !!! (26.06.2014) |publisher=YouTube |date=}}</ref> On 4 July, he stated that he is "not an enemy of Atatürk," and that "incorporating religion into politics will lead to trouble."<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.haber7.com/roportaj/haber/1176363-ekmeleddin-ihsanoglu-laikligi-savunuyorum |title=Ekmeleddin İhsanoğlu: Laikliği savunuyorum – RÖPORTAJ Haberleri |publisher=Haber7.com |date=}}</ref> Former CHP leader [[Deniz Baykal]], who was seen as a potential CHP nominee, criticised İhsanoğlu's candidacy, stating that the CHP and MHP should have held a vote amongst their members to chose a candidate.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.egedesonsoz.com/haber/Baykal-dan-cok-sert-cati-aday-aciklamalari/872174 |title=Baykal dan çok sert çatı aday açıklamaları |publisher=Egedesonsoz.com |date=23 June 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.erkenhaberal.com/baykaldancati-aday-icin-ilk-tepki/ |title=Baykalâ€™danâ€™Ă§atÄą adayâ€™ iĂ§in ilk tepki |publisher=ErkenHaberAl |date=14 May 2014}}</ref>

On 7 July, İhsanoğlu stated that he would not base his campaign on election rallies, stating, "how right is it to force people outside under the heat in this holy month of [[Ramadan]]? When are we going to hold the rallies, before [[sahur]] or after [[iftar]]? We are visiting our provinces and districts, meeting local leaders and visiting our people." He also expressed his wish to hold a live televised debate with Erdoğan.<ref>{{cite web|author=Barış Yarkadaş |url=http://www.gercekgundem.com/siyaset/55278/iste-ihsanoglunun-miting-yapmama-nedeni |title=İşte İhsanoğlu'nun miting yapmama nedeni – Gerçek Gündem |publisher=Gercekgundem.com |date=}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.samanyoluhaber.com/politika/Ekmeleddin-Ihsanoglu-neden-miting-yapmadigini-acikladi/1056479/ |title=İhsanoğlu: Mübarek Ramazan'da insanlara mitingle neden zulmedelim? Haberleri, En Son Haber |publisher=Samanyolu Haber |date=}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.avrupagazete.com/mobile/turkiye/92903-ekmeleddin-ihsanoglu-nun-miting-yapmama-nedeni.html |title=Ekmeleddin İhsanoğlu'nun miting yapmama nedeni &#124; AVR |publisher=Avrupagazete.com |date=10 July 2014}}</ref> Following the conclusion of Ramadan, İhsanoğlu held his first election rally in [[Hatay]] on 2 August, reiterating his support for state secularism.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://videonuz.ensonhaber.com/izle/ekmeleddin-ihsanoglu-ilk-kez-hatay-da-miting-yapti |title=Ekmeleddin İhsanoğlu ilk kez Hatay'da miting yaptı |publisher=Videonuz.ensonhaber.com |date=2 August 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.ensonhaber.com/ekmeleddin-ihsanoglu-ilk-kez-hatayda-miting-yapti-2014-08-02.html |title=Ekmeleddin İhsanoğlu ilk kez Hatay'da miting yaptı |publisher=En son haber |date=2 August 2014}}</ref> İhsanoğlu's campaign slogan is "''Ekmek için Ekmeleddin''" (''Ekmeleddin for bread''), other slogans which will be used for the campaign include "Ekmeleddin to cultivate love, to cultivate prosperity and for bread." "Ekmek" means "to cultivate" at the same time.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.dailysabah.com/politics/2014/07/10/ihsanoglu-announces-his-election-campaign-program |title=İhsanoğlu announces his election campaign program &#124; Politics |publisher=Daily Sabah |date=}}</ref>

[[File:2014 Turkish Presidential Election campaign.jpg|thumb|left|Posters of candidates Erdoğan, Demirtaş and İhsanoğlu in [[Mecidiyeköy]], [[Istanbul]]]]
Following Erdoğan's accusation that İhsanoğlu did not know the [[Independence March]], İhsanoğlu responded by saying that since the author of the March, [[Mehmet Akif Ersoy]] was the best friend of his father, he had already learnt the anthem as a baby.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.zaman.com.tr/politika_ekmeleddin-ihsanoglu-istiklal-marsi-mevzuu-yanlis-yansitildi_2235160.html |title=Ekmeleddin İhsanoğlu: İstiklal Marşı mevzuu yanlış yansıtıldı |publisher=ZAMAN |date=}}</ref> In a statement, he claimed that the video that Erdoğan showed during his [[Kahramanmaraş]] rally was "doctored," and that he had "translated this unrivalled piece into [[Arabic]], how is it possible that I wouldn't know it?"<ref>http://www.cumhuriyet.com.tr/haber/turkiye/100717/ihsanoglu_ndan_istiklal_Marsi_aciklamasi.html</ref> On 2 August, the pro-opposition newspaper [[Sözcü]] published footage of Recep Tayyip Erdoğan himself misreading the Independence March.<ref>{{cite web|author=Ağustos 2, 2014 | |url=http://sozcu.com.tr/2014/gundem/erdoganda-istiklal-marsini-yanlis-okumus-568963/ |title=Erdoğan'da istiklal Marşı'nı yanlış okumuş!- Sözcü Gazetesi |publisher=Sozcu.com.tr |date=2 August 2014}}</ref>

On 16 July, İhsanoğlu visited the Palestinian embassy in [[Ankara]], denying reports that he had said on 4 July that [[Turkey]] should remain "neutral" in in the Israeli-Palestinian issue.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.haber7.com/televizyon/haber/1176287-ihsanoglundan-sok-filistin-ve-israil-yorumu |title=İhsanoğlu'ndan şok Filistin ve İsrail yorumu – Televizyon Haberleri |publisher=Haber7.com |date=}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://gundem.bugun.com.tr/noktayi-boyle-koydu-haberi/1187558 |title=Ekmeleddin İhsanoğlu'ndan Filistin açıklaması |publisher=Gundem.bugun.com.tr |date=}}</ref> In a statement, he said that "I have never advocated Turkish neutrality. You cannot be neutral between the cruel and the oppressed."<ref>{{cite web|url=http://hergunmedya.com/haber/ekmeleddin-ihsanoglu-filistin-devleti-buyukelciligini-ziyaret-etti/6439/ |title=Ekmeleddin İhsanoğlu Filistin Devleti Büyükelçiliği'ni ziyaret etti &#124; Haberler > SİYASET |publisher=Hergunmedya.com |date=16 July 2014}}</ref> On 19 July, he stated that Palestine should take their case to the [[International Criminal Court]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.haberturk.com/gundem/haber/971519-ihsanoglu-filistin-uluslararasi-ceza-mahkemesine-gitmeli |title=İhsanoğlu: Filistin Uluslararası Ceza Mahkemesi'ne gitmeli |publisher=Haberturk.com |date=19 July 2014}}</ref>

In his vision, İhsanoğlu vowed to protect democracy, the rule of law, the separation of powers, the principles of Atatürk and national unity. He also advocated waiving the debts of Turkey's poorest citizens. He further stressed the need for greater involvement of non-governmental organisations as well as local authorities in the decision making process in order to strengthen democracy. In addition, he stresses the importance of environmental protection, greater rights to women and educational assistance to the nation's poorest children in order to turn Turkey into a "nation of knowledge" such as [[South Korea]]. İhsanoğlu states that because he is not the candidate of a single party, he would be able to solve national tensions between the opposition and government as well as bring about peace and stability to both Turkey and to the world through foreign policy.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://ihsanoglu.com/vizyon/ |title=Vizyonu &#124; Ekmeleddin İhsanoğlu |publisher=Ihsanoglu.com |date=20 June 2014}}</ref>

===Demirtaş campaign===

Selahattin Demirtaş was announced as a candidate for the Presidency on 30 June.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.ntvmsnbc.com/id/25523738/ |title=HDP'nin adayı Selahattin Demirtaş – Türkiye |publisher=ntvmsnbc.com |date=1 January 1970}}</ref> In a campaign dominated by the "peace process" with Kurdish rebels, he claimed on 5 August in [[Van (Turkey)|Van]] that the government of Recep Tayyip Erdoğan had not done enough to bring forward promised legislation, and that the process would collapse immediately if the AKP did not do more to bring lasting peace in the southeast.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.milliyet.com.tr/demirtas-baris-surecinin/siyaset/detay/1921365/default.htm |title=Demirtaş: Barış sürecinin bozulmaması gerekir – Milliyet Haber |publisher=Milliyet.com.tr |date=}}</ref> He is the co-leader of the [[Peoples' Democratic Party (Turkey)|Peoples' Democratic Party]] (HDP), serving alongside [[Figen Yüksekdağ]].

On 15 July, Demirtaş outlined his road-map for his presidency should he win the election. In a speech lasting just under an hour, he proposed that the [[Ministry of Religious Affairs]] (Diyanet) should be disbanded, that compulsory religion lessons in schools should be removed and that [[Cemevi]]s (the [[Alevi]] houses of worship) should receive national recognition.<ref name="yurtgazetesi1">{{cite web|url=http://www.yurtgazetesi.com.tr/politika/diyanet-kaldirilmali-cemevleri-yasal-statuye-kavusturulmali-h56640.html |title='Diyanet kaldırılmalı, cemevleri yasal statüye kavuşturulmalı' |publisher=Yurtgazetesi.com.tr |date=}}</ref> He also proposed the introduction of "People's Parliaments" ''(Cumhur meclisleri)'', which would also incorporate Youth Parliaments to increase representation of young citizens.<ref>{{cite web|author=Temmuz 15, 2014 | |url=http://sozcu.com.tr/2014/gundem/demirtastan-turk-bayragi-mesaji-556375/ |title=Demirtaş'tan Türk bayrağı mesajı- Sözcü Gazetesi |publisher=Sozcu.com.tr |date=15 July 2014}}</ref> Pushing for a new constitution, Demirtaş outlined the need to end the non-representation of different cultures, languages, races and beliefs without delay to ensure national stability.<ref>{{cite web|author=ali |url=http://www.wanhaber.com/selahattin-demirtas-yol-haritasini-acikladi-193637h.htm |title=Selahattin Demirtaş Yol Haritasını Açıkladı |publisher=Wanhaber.com |date=15 July 2014}}</ref> Also in his speech, he praised the [[Gezi Park protests]] and displayed photos of himself during the events. He continued to direct applause to the mother of the murdered teenager [[Berkin Elvan]], who died 269 days after being hit by a tear gas canister during the protests and falling into a coma.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.dunya.com/demirtas-kosk-icin-yol-haritasini-acikladi-233457h.htm |title=Demirtaş Köşk için yol haritasını açıkladı |publisher=Dunya.com |date=15 July 2014}}</ref> On the issue of the lack of Turkish flags within the hall in which he was delivering his speech, Demirtaş stated that the Turkish flag represented all citizens of Turkey.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.turkiyegazetesi.com.tr/politika/171293.aspx |title=Demirtaş yol haritasını açıkladı – TG |publisher=Turkiyegazetesi.com.tr |date=15 July 2014}}</ref> His slogan is ''"Bir Cumhurbaşkanı Düşün" (Imagine a President...)'', which is followed by several different phrases, such as ''"Bir Cumhurbaşkanı Düşünün Ayrımcılık yapmıyor. Birleştiriyor, barıştırıyor." (Imagine a President who doesn't Discriminate, who Unites and makes Peace)'' or ''"Bir Cumhurbaşkanı Düşünün Herkese Demokrat" (Imagine a President who is Democratic to Everybody).''<ref name="yurtgazetesi1"/>

On 18 July, Demirtaş visited Paris, France, and laid flowers at the scene where three Kurdish activists were shot dead on 9 January 2013.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://t24.com.tr/haber/selahattin-demirtas-pariste-3-pkklinin-olduruldugu-yere-cicek-birakti,264833 |title=Selahattin Demirtaş Paris'te 3 PKK'lının öldürüldüğü yere çiçek bıraktı – Politika |publisher=T24 |date=}}</ref>

