==Conduct==

===Overseas voting===
Voting overseas began on 31 July and ended on 3 August. 2,783,660 overseas citizens were eligible to vote in 54 countries, and voting took place in 103 consulates.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://gundem.bugun.com.tr/sandiklar-bos-kaldi-haberi/1211193 |title=Yurt dışındaki 10 seçmenden sadece 1'i sandığa gitti |publisher=Gundem.bugun.com.tr |date=}}</ref> Voting at borders and customs started on 26 July and continued until 10 August.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.hurriyet.com.tr/avrupa/26944847.asp |title=İşte yurt dışında kullanılan oy sayısı – Hürriyet Avrupa |publisher=Hurriyet.com.tr |date=}}</ref> On 4 August, Deputy Prime Minister [[Emrullah İşler]] announced that 232,000 overseas voters cast their votes, with a turnout of 8.5%, while votes cast at borders and customs had reached 152,000.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.mansettv.com/haber/isler-kesin-rakam-veriyorum-133370.html |title=İşler: Kesin rakam veriyorum |publisher=Mansettv.com |date=}}</ref> With the low turnout being attributed to the requirement to book an appointment to vote, it had previously emerged on 30 July that only 248,285 voters booked an appointment.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.hurriyet.com.tr/dunya/26909626.asp |title=Gurbetçi oyunda randevu şoku – Hürriyet DÜNYA |publisher=Hurriyet.com.tr |date=30 July 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.haberler.com/yurtdisindaki-secmene-randevu-soku-6320913-haberi/ |title=Yurtdışındaki Seçmene Randevu Şoku |publisher=Haberler.com |date=30 July 2014}}</ref> It was seen as a setback for Recep Tayyip Erdoğan, who had been predicted half of the overseas vote.<ref name="todayszaman1"/> On 5 August, the owner of A&G research company Adil Gür stated that the overseas vote wouldn't affect Erdoğan's chances of success.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.internethaber.com/kazanmak-icin-yurtdisi-oylarina-gerek-yok-706860h.htm |title=Kazanmak için yurtdışı oylarına gerek yok! haberi |publisher=Internethaber.com |date=}}</ref>

